.TH ORPHAND-SNAPS 8 "2025-12-09" "orphand-snaps" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
orphand-snaps \- remove orphaned and disabled snap packages, with undo support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B orphand-snaps
.RI [ undo " [" SNAPNAME " | all ]" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The orphand-snaps script:
- Removes disabled snaps and orphaned content/base snaps if safe to delete.
- Records removed snaps from the last run in
.I /var/lib/orphand-snaps/last_removed.txt
to support undo.
- Installs a systemd oneshot service and weekly timer (via package installation).
.PP
When run as a regular user without arguments, the script attempts to remove snaps 
using elevated privileges (doas or sudo). The elevation method is auto-detected; 
override with
.B OVERRIDE_ELEVATION=doas|sudo
.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B "orphand-snaps"
Run the cleanup (removes disabled and orphaned snaps).
.TP
.B "undo"
List snaps removed in the last run.
.TP
.B "undo SNAPNAME"
Restore a single snap (uses snap refresh/install; revision if recorded).
.TP
.B "undo all"
Restore all snaps recorded in the last run.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/local/bin/orphand-snaps
\- installed script
.br
.I /etc/systemd/system/orphand-snaps.service
.br
.I /etc/systemd/system/orphand-snaps.timer
.br
.I /var/lib/orphand-snaps/last_removed.txt
\- state file (name,channel,revision)
.SH EXAMPLES
Manual cleanup: orphand-snaps
.br
Undo list: orphand-snaps undo
.br
Undo one: orphand-snaps undo core18
.br
Undo all: orphand-snaps undo all
.br
Override elevation: OVERRIDE_ELEVATION=doas orphand-snaps undo
.SH NOTES
The package installs a systemd timer that runs the cleanup automatically once per week.
.br
When invoked as a non-root user, the script requires either
.B sudo
or
.B doas
to be available in PATH.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR snap (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
